  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 5aa0de718882e0e4fb6bbb67eec1d13f, type: 3}
  m_Name: Phase3_Parallel
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::STEM.Experiments.Resistance.ResistancePhase
  instruction: 'Step 3: Rearrange the cables so R1 is connected

    in parallel
    with R2. The ammeter stays in series,

    the voltmeter in parallel across R1.'
  resultText: 'Measurement: V = {V} V, I = {I} A


    Total resistance: Rtot = V
    / I = {Vn} / {In} = {R} Ohm


    1/R = 1/R1 + 1/R2 = 1/100 + 1/50  ->  R = 33.33
    Ohm


    The total resistance is smaller than either resistor,

    because
    the current has more paths to flow through.'
  requiredTopology: 3
  requiredVoltmeter: 1
  switchStartsClosed: 1
